WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.800
Hey everyone, привет, welcome to привет русский эпизод 25,

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:07.220
it's 16th May, 2026 года.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:11.340
I'm Olya, and today we're going to learn some really fun Russian words.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:14.000
Ready, poехали, that means let's go.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.700
Today's special word is pagoda, pagoda, it means weather.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:23.900
pagoda sounds just like good day, and that makes it perfect for talking about nice weather.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:28.860
Say it slowly with me, pagoda, now again at normal speed, pagoda.

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:31.340
We can use it in a sentence like this.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:36.640
Сегодня хорошая pagoda, that means today the weather is good, repeat after me.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:38.740
Сегодня хорошая pagoda.

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:42.700
Now let's add more words that help us talk about the weather every day.

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:46.580
The first one is солнце, солнце, that means sun.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:51.580
Think of solar panels that catch power from the sun, and you will remember солнце.

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:53.420
Repeat after me, солнце.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.040
Here is how we use it.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:58.840
солнце светит ярко, that means the sun is shining brightly.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:02.400
Next comes dожд, dожд, it means rain.

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:07.700
Picture raindrops dождик down from the sky, and the sound of dожд will stick in your mind.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:13.380
Repeat after me, dожд, we say it like this, idiot dожд, that means it is raining.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:17.480
Now we have снег, снег, that means snow.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:21.600
снег sounds almost exactly like snow, and the two words are really cousins.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.400
Repeat after me, снег.

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:29.580
A simple sentence is this, zie мой падает снег, that means in winter snow falls.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:34.760
The next word is тепло, тепло, it means warmth or warm.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:39.100
тепли feels like toasty and warm overall into one cozy word.

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:44.380
Repeat after me, тепло, we use it like this, this noise становится тепло.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.340
That means in spring it becomes warm.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:54.120
Then we have холодно, холодно, that means cold, холодно starts with the English word cold,

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:56.040
and just adds a Russian ending.

00:01:56.540 --> 00:01:58.220
Repeat after me, холодно.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:03.920
A sentence we can say is, sevотне холодно, that means today it is cold.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:08.240
One more weather word is ветер, ветер, it means wind.

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:13.340
ветер sounds like ветер, an old wind that has been blowing for a very long time.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.340
Repeat after me, ветер.

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:20.600
We can say, sirne ветер, do it, that means a strong wind is blowing.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:24.560
Finally, we have visna, visna, it means spring.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:29.300
Visna feels like fresh and new, just like the flowers that bloom in spring.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:31.500
Repeat after me, visna.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:36.020
A happy sentence is, visna пришла, that means spring has arrived.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:40.340
Now here is a simple grammar tip that helps us talk about the weather in Russian.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:45.100
We add a special ending all to certain words when we describe the weather.

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:49.300
Look at these examples, sevотне тепло, today it is warm,

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:52.380
and sevотне холодно, today it is cold.

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:57.820
English just says it is cold, but Russian adds that little all to show we mean the weather,

00:02:58.240 --> 00:02:59.280
not a person or thing.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:03.440
Once you know this, you can say many weather sentences right away.

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:08.420
In Russia, people love talking about the weather because winter has last a long time

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:09.600
and stay very cold.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:15.860
When visna finally arrives, everyone celebrates the return of warmth and the first flowers after months

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:18.860
of snow. Let's practice what we learned.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:24.300
Look out the window right now and try saying sevотне with one of our new words.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:30.160
If you are drawing a picture of today's weather, label it with солнце, dorscht or снег.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:34.340
You just use the real Russian sentences about the weather, that is fantastic.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:37.960
Now here's something really cool about one of today's words.

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:40.540
Want to know a secret about снег?

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:44.820
Did you know that the Russian word снег and the English word snow

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:47.280
are actually the same ancient word?

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.280
They both come from a very old language spoken thousands of years ago called

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:58.700
Proto-Indo-European. That word started as снег-w and traveled through many languages,

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:04.240
slowly changing its sound until it became снег in Russian and snow in English.

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:10.320
But be careful, the Russian word magazine sounds like magazine, but actually means shock.

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:14.940
Next time you see snow falling, remember it is cousins with a snake.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.580
They both come from the same magical root.

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:21.080
That connection is your secret shortcut to remembering it forever.

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:23.400
Moladets, that means well done.

